  "description_html": "Life restoration of the gigantic Late Cretaceous caenagnathid <i>Beibeilong sinensis</i>. The large-sized eggs and embryonic specimen (Baby Louie) assigned to this taxon indicate a notorious adult size comparable to <i>Gigantoraptor</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The robust body proportions depicted in this restoration are mostly based on <i>Gigantoraptor</i> and also Baby Louie (especially hindlimbs), based on the reasoning that some oviraptorosaurs retained limb proportions in their ontogeny.<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Since the both taxa feature similar hindlimb ratios despite their age, it is possible to use the more mature <i>Gigantoraptor</i> for other body regions as a primary reference.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2017). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5477524\">Perinate and eggs of a giant caenagnathid dinosaur from the Late Cretaceous of central China</a>\". <i>Nature Communications</i> <b>8</b>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms14952\">10.1038/ncomms14952</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMID</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28486442\">28486442</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed_Central\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed Central\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMC</span></a></span>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5477524\">5477524</a>.</cite> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms14952/MediaObjects/41467_2017_BFncomms14952_MOESM553_ESM.pdf\">Supplementary Information</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2013). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dinoweb.ucoz.ru/_fr/17/Chicken-sized_o.pdf\">Chicken-sized oviraptorid dinosaurs from central China and their ontogenetic implications</a>\". <i>Naturwissenschaften</i> <b>100</b> (2): 165–175. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00114-012-1007-0\">10.1007/s00114-012-1007-0</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMID</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23314810\">23314810</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(2007). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/6272413\">A gigantic bird-like dinosaur from the Late Cretaceous of China</a>\". <i>Nature</i> <b>447</b> (7146): 844−847. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature05849\">10.1038/nature05849</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMID</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17565365\">17565365</a>.</cite> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05849/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05849_MOESM353_ESM.pdf\">Supplementary Information</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
